WEBVTT

00:00:08,910 --> 00:00:16,350
Do you see any value in a daily shot with the ingredients of juice of what organic lemon?

00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:27,550
One tablespoon, good olive oil. One teaspoon black seed oil. I don't see any problem with that.

00:00:28,510 --> 00:00:33,870
The only caveat to that would be you're taking a tablespoon of olive oil.

00:00:34,430 --> 00:00:41,630
If a person doesn't have a gallbladder, that could be an issue, but if they have a gallbladder,

00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:44,990
that could help their gallbladder flush, so that could actually be helpful.

00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:49,710
I don't see any problem with that at all, so there's no negatives to that.

00:00:50,590 --> 00:00:56,350
Do I know of a good olive oil? Well, you can go back and forth on all sorts of different

00:00:57,150 --> 00:01:01,790
philosophies of what good olive oil is and that's not good olive oil.

00:01:02,990 --> 00:01:08,670
It's just really hard to kind of wade through that muck.

00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:15,790
I would just try to buy an organic olive oil and it's always good to try to buy one that's from

00:01:15,790 --> 00:01:21,870
a single source. If you look on the back and it says product of Italy, then you know it's coming

00:01:21,870 --> 00:01:29,950
from Italy. If it says product of Italy, Spain, and Portugal, then it's a mixed olive oil that they

00:01:29,950 --> 00:01:37,070
may be cutting it with cheaper versions, so you'll want it to be a single source olive oil.

00:01:37,070 --> 00:01:43,870
I know there's some places in olive vineyards in California where you can buy olive oil

00:01:43,870 --> 00:01:50,830
straight from them. It's coming from one vineyard and I think you can get that from places in

00:01:50,830 --> 00:02:04,350
Italy too. That's what I would at least have been taught to look for. It makes sense to me.

